{"rpid": "3737383079", "root": "0", "parent": "0", "uname": "InmostCalm", "mid": "9044", "level": 6, "vip": 1, "content": "The music video for \"Warwick Avenue\" premiered on 23 April 2008, on Channel 4 and was directed by Daniel Wolfe. The video is almost entirely composed of a single shot; it starts with Duffy leaving Warwick Avenue tube station in the back of a black taxi, crying as she is singing the song. The video finishes with Duffy still in the car, wiping her tears, which had ruined her make-up. The taxi scene was only meant to be one scene from the whole video but the director felt that it was best to use this scene only when Duffy cried real tears. He continued to film it as the whole music video.\n\nThe video was later nominated for a MTV Video Music Award in 2008 in the Best UK Video category,【5】 but lost to \"Shut Up and Let Me Go\" by the Ting Tings.", "like": 5, "ctime": 1606070112, "rcount": 0, "ip": "", "images": [], "video_aid": "175406", "video_bvid": "BV1Ex411w7KD", "video_title": "【经典】Duffy-Warwick Avenue", "video_desc": "新浪 这首歌循环好多次了……真的很棒！", "video_owner": "艾柔玛", "video_view": 6826, "video_reply": 16, "video_n1": 10, "video_n2": 6}
